Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 10 17:20:42 2026 +1100

    l3: Report pending updates in agent state
    
    The L3 agent queues router and network updates for its worker pool, but
    nothing shows how long that queue is without reading the agent's logs.
    Report its length as pending_updates in the configurations the agent
    sends with every heartbeat, beside its router and interface counts.
    
    Prompt: while reading the L3 agent, Mikal asked whether it publishes any
    metrics about its work queue. It does not, and LP #1512864 left such
    instrumentation to case-by-case patches, so he chose to propose the
    smallest in-tree change first and see how reviewers react.
    Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context, low effort) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context, low effort) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
    Change-Id: Icb83a84cc95388c9f68af538294022730dca1b90
    Signed-off-by: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>

